What is it?
​OWASP stands for the Open Web Application Security Project. It’s a global non-profit organization that works to improve software security.
​The Top 10 is their flagship report. It isn't just a random list—it's a data-driven consensus from security experts worldwide about the 10 most critical web application security risks.
​Why does it matter for us?
​For Pentesters: It’s your checklist. When I'm working in my lab on Parrot OS, these are the first things I look for.
​For Developers: It’s your shield. Knowing these helps you write code that is "Secure by Design."
